Chosen deliberately over a permissive license: GPL-3.0's copyleft
requires anyone who distributes a modified or combined version of this
software to release their source under the same terms, and its
anti-tivoization provisions specifically prevent shipping this code
inside a locked-down device that prevents the end user from installing
their own modified build — a real, relevant scenario for driver code
running on physical hardware, which a permissive license would not have
stopped.

